WEBVTT

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.880
Wh-what... What the heck?!

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:28.380
Requesting your name and affiliation, please.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.170
Wh-what? A robot?! Hey, let me go!

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.130
Let go of me!

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:38.210
Suspicious...

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:40.920
I-I'm not some suspicious guy!

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:51.130
Now, get a load of this! Sometimes,
I'm a hotel waiter, sometimes I'm a taxi driver,

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:54.580
and still other times I'm a babysitter.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.290
However, at my core...

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:02.830
I'm private detective Kensaku Ban!

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:09.580
Definitely suspicious...

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:12.790
Your name and affiliation.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:36.670
A clear sky should look blue for me, too, and yet

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:43.170
My uncertain heart, and also the love that you gave me

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:46.830
For someone who finds a way to lose like me

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.330
They are an existence that constitutes an error

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:53.580
Even without a single mistake

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.380
Look! Proof it is correct

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:00.790
It certainly does not result in

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:03.040
For which even the title is not set

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.500
Log data that is already unknown

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:10.040
We are still on the other side of the puddle

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.130
Is it affection? Is it heartlessness?

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:15.630
How many times I've tried to extract it, I cannot know

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:21.000
It seems like something is going to pour out

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.960
The indecipherable runs down my cheek

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:31.460
Leave me alone, okay?

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.380
Like I said...

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:47.880
I'm not some suspicious guy!

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.710
That's generally what suspicious guys say.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:53.210
Suspicious...

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:56.000
O-o-ow! Hey, cut it out!

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.290
Don't pull on my trademark moustache like that!

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:02.290
A106, examine this man.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:03.540
Understood.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:06.580
I will analyze the condition of his sweat.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.250
Ugh! Don't you dare do anything gross like that!

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.210
Hello!

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.250
Huh?

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:17.500
Hiroshi, what are you doing with that girl?!

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.920
How rude! I was planning on setting you up
with a part-time job, you know...

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:24.670
Y-Young Lady?!

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:25.710
Oh my!

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:29.880
Young Lady, please tell this guy that I'm a detective!

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.380
Is he really a detective?

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:36.130
Rather than a detective per se...
I suppose he's a jack of all trades?

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:39.130
A suspicious jack of all trades...

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:44.000
Like I said, I was simply searching for Malon!

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.210
Malon...

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:52.540
You mean this thing here?

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:55.710
Yep, the very-much-lost Malon.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.040
How ridiculous.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.380
Is this...?

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.750
Huh, what?

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.500
Oh, this thing? Hmm...

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:04.500
Look!

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.170
A robot...

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.580
Isn't that thing just a pet robot from a bygone age?

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:13.420
What's the deal with it?

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.540
The client considers her
something of a keepsake, you see.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.710
It seems he would like for her to be found at any cost.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.170
So why'd you come to this university?

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:25.040
It seems that somehow or other
she has taken refuge here.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:28.500
Our campus is rather large.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.830
Who knows how long it would take a single person...?

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:33.670
That's where I get to show off my skill as a detective!

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:35.920
There is a reward being offered, right?

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:36.830
Yes.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:38.960
Oh, and it's pretty big...

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:43.500
You know, these guys have blown through their budget
and are looking for part-time work...

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:46.880
As students here, they of course
know the campus well...

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:49.710
Hey, why don't you hire them?

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:52.960
Eh?! Motoko-san, isn't that a bit too sudden?!

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:57.000
The money seems to be better than the job
I was going to introduce you to, anyway.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:00.790
With a reward this high,
we can make everyone here part of the team.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.080
But amateurs simply aren't cut out for this...

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:07.420
I believe there will be no reward at all
if you don't actually find her...

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:11.960
Well, it is true sheer force of numbers
is fundamental to an investigation.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:15.000
Um... if you don't include us in the discussion...

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.080
Very well, then!

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.500
I'll take you up on that part-time job!

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.750
Eh? But earlier didn't you say this is ridiculous?

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:26.170
We upped the sensitivity of A106's sensors, didn't we?

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:27.000
Yeah...

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.420
I want to test them out.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:33.080
I see! If we use Six to search for the pet robot,
we'll find her no problem!

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:36.460
NO WAY!

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:39.500
Don't take being a detective so lightly!

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:45.130
Putting the client first during an investigation...
That is something only a human can do!

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.040
The trade requires one's heart and soul!

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:51.330
Yes, the heart. It's a trade where having a heart is vital.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.920
The thought of entrusting the job to that
heartless piece of junk...

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.790
I adamantly oppose it!

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:00.830
Delicious!

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.630
Thank you.

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:05.170
Ugh!

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:08.790
In the first place, letting this piece of junk-!

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:14.540
Hold up! We made A106, so do you really
want to be calling him a piece of junk like that?

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:17.540
Being a detective is impossible
for a piece of junk like that!

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:21.540
Alright, then how about a little contest with A106?!

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:22.750
Say what?!

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:28.290
That little lost robot...
Let's see who finds it first: you or A106!

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:32.500
If I win, I get the privilege of shaving off
that moustache of yours!

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.040
Wh-what's that now?!

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.880
Well, how about if you lose?

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:38.460
You'll get a whole month's labor for free...

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:39.330
...from Hiroshi.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:41.460
Eh?! Hey, wait a minute!

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:43.040
Alright, it's a deal!

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:43.710
Gotcha.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.290
Listen here! An investigation requires hitting the streets.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:49.330
The one who does some old-fashioned legwork
will be victorious in the end!

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:50.380
Oh yeah?

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:53.580
Be that as it may...

00:06:55.630 --> 00:07:00.920
He may call it old-fashioned legwork,
but isn't it nothing more than walking around blindly?

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:05.960
Come on! You better really search now!
Otherwise I'm not paying ya!

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:08.750
Okay, I hear you!

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:10.710
Hey, Ochanomizu-kun,

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:14.830
why is it that we have to search with that guy?

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.750
We have no choice.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:22.540
Umataro decided it's best this way so that Maruhige-san
can't blame losing on being outnumbered later.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.500
Over here we've got you, Motoko-san,
along with myself and Maruhige-san,

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:30.380
and over there they've got Umataro, Ran, and Six...
so it's three vs. three.

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:32.580
It's relatively well-balanced, huh?

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:37.000
Jeez, why is it that men are always so childish like this?

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:38.250
Hey!

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:42.130
It seems she's not over here either.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:44.960
We've finished searching all of the main areas now...

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:47.630
In that case, perhaps she really is
in one of the campus buildings.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:50.130
You're lucky to have us with you, huh?

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:53.630
Those who aren't affiliated with the university
can't go inside the buildings, after all.

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:58.380
That being the case, shouldn't you
be able to garner a higher wage?

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:03.920
Still, putting up so much money
to track this thing down...

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.170
That pet robot must be pretty darn important to him.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.920
It doesn't look all that valuable, though.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:13.920
The manufacturer changed course.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:18.420
With production now discontinued,
it commands a premium as an antique.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.170
Oh, so that's it.

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:21.920
Was it stolen or something?

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:23.920
Don't know.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:29.790
The owner tried everything he could, but it seems
he gave up when he couldn't find her anywhere.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:31.790
However...

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:39.540
A few days ago, his pet suddenly received a signal
which he had presumed was gone forever.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:48.130
And that transmission came from here
at National Nerima University?

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:49.080
Yes.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:52.830
Hmm... There sure are
a lot of buildings here on campus...

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:55.330
In any case, we have to put in the legwork and search!

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:57.630
Come on, let's go!

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:01.330
Will we find her?

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:03.540
Detection in progress...

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:04.830
For what?

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.500
He's analyzing its network protocol.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:13.540
The protocol that pet robot uses may have been
the latest at the time, but now it's a relic.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:15.880
He'll be able to identify it in no time.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:16.960
Hmm...

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:21.420
At the very least, we'll get a hit
so long as it's somewhere on campus.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:25.250
Well, the sensor was originally meant
for tracking down "that thing," though.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:26.500
"That thing"?

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.750
It was present in A106's records...

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:30.250
This thing!

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:34.130
It's not clear where it's from,
but that thing is definitely autonomous...

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:37.250
It's a robot that was created with
quite a high level of technological knowhow.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:40.500
In terms of who could actually create it...

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:45.000
Moriya Tsutsumi.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:47.500
That guy my brother often praises...

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:51.330
Hmph! I garner more praise than that guy.

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:52.670
Childish...

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:54.420
Don't tell Hiroshi about this.

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:55.250
'Kay.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:58.210
Still, this is taking quite a long time...

00:09:58.210 --> 00:09:59.210
Failure...

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:01.250
I'm not capable of failure!

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:02.830
Overconfident...

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.790
That's simply a proper evaluation!

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:07.790
Detection complete.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:09.290
Alright!

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:10.540
So where is she?!

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:15.630
Within Nerima University: 2,594 hits.

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:16.960
Narrow it down!

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:21.290
Within a radius of one meter: 1 hit.

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:22.790
Nonsense!

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:24.670
Right here.

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:25.540
What?

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:32.380
That's...!

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:35.880
That's a cheap, low-spec model
from multiple generations ago!

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:40.880
Trying to see how useful you can make something
while customizing it under limits, huh?

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.920
That's something that any engineering enthusiast
has probably tried once!

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:46.460
Yeah, it's a hand-me-down from my brother.

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:49.580
So there must be other people
still using those things, too.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:56.460
I see! This network protocol
is also used by that type of mobile device!

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:01.500
Jeez, where in the world did those two go?

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:04.710
Don't tell me that Ochanomizu-kun and that man
have gotten lost too now!

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:06.170
As if!

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:11.460
I'm sorry about that...

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.040
I'm the one who should be apologizing.

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:20.170
It has been quite some time since I've been here,
and I managed to lose my way...

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:20.960
Hm?

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:23.960
Excuse me, what's that over there?

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:27.460
They've been doing construction
over there since last month.

00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:30.210
There's often quite a bit of construction
going on at the university.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:34.130
So, you can't head over to the other side
without taking a bit of a detour.

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:36.250
Is that right...?

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:40.500
Now you understand what searching in earnest means!

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:41.500
There they are!

00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:44.250
I'm in a bit of a hurry, so I'll be seeing you!

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:02.000
Hmm... Where are you? Where could you be?

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:05.500
Hey, Malon!

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:07.750
Malon, where are you?!

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:14.880
Twenty-seven thousand...?

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:18.500
That's three days' worth of walking already.
I'm gonna be exhausted.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.540
There you are!

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:23.290
Considering we're on the same team, don't you think
it's pretty awful to leave me behind like that?!

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:27.080
Sorry, my bad. I just got so caught up in the search.

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:28.630
No leads yet?

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:29.790
Nope...

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:31.330
Alright!

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:33.000
Hey, Malon!

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:35.290
You're really going at it, huh?

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:40.130
If we find her, that means you have
to work for free for a month, you know.

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:43.790
Well, I couldn't help remembering something
that happened a long time ago.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:45.000
A long time ago?

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:46.540
Quite some time ago,

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:49.880
I had a similar type of pet robot
that I received as a hand-me-down.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.080
I really loved that thing.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:56.830
It had this feature where if you'd call its name,
it would head over to you.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:59.330
So that's why you keep calling her name...

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:03.250
Also, giving it a name makes you start to feel attached...

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:05.330
I cried when it broke.

00:13:05.670 --> 00:13:11.580
Thinking about that, I started to feel bad for the client,
who had clearly cherished his pet.

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:18.210
People on campus who have mobile devices
from three generations ago...

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:21.830
No way... You detected all of these?

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:24.830
Two-thousand five-hundred ninety-four people...

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:26.500
How will we search for her?

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.790
One hit eliminated.

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:34.330
Currently, 2,593 hits.

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:37.130
Three additional hits.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:38.130
Currently-

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:41.630
Gah, stop that! There's no need to count off each hit!

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:43.000
Understood.

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:44.880
I've got it.

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:46.380
What is it?

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:50.500
Mobile devices are something
you take with you as you move around.

00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:52.170
Obviously.

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:54.170
Does that pet move?

00:13:54.170 --> 00:13:57.250
Well, if it's broken...

00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:59.000
Ah, that's it!

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:03.540
A106, narrow it down to devices
that haven't moved in a while!

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:04.630
Understood.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:06.540
Come on now...

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:08.330
Detection complete.

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:10.130
Fifty-one hits.

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:13.130
We don't have that much time...

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:17.040
Okay, from here on out, let's move around
as we continue working on it!

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.920
Ah, I can't keep going any longer!

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:23.920
I can't believe a young'n like you is already tired out!

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:28.170
It's not like we're going to find her
using such primitive methods anyway...

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:31.170
If you give up, you lose
the possibility of making progress.

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:34.040
It's important to have faith at all times.

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:36.170
You have to believe we'll surely find her!

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:38.960
I've had enough already! I don't believe that!

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:43.210
I mean, if she fell into a hole or something,

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:45.670
there'd be no point in searching
above ground, would there?

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:47.210
Ah, I see...

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:50.130
Right?! This is pointless!

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:53.420
Ten meters to go.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:56.710
Nine meters to go.

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:58.250
We're close now!

00:14:58.250 --> 00:14:59.750
Eight meters...

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.250
Is that it?!

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:06.290
Oh?

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:08.790
Response detected from inside the bag.

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:10.330
What's inside that bag?!

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:13.330
Eh? What's inside, you ask?

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:20.380
We did it! I'm the winner!

00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:23.210
We have been searching for that robot!

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:25.210
For this...?

00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:31.460
I came to take a look when I heard some guy
yelling like an idiot - big surprise it was you.

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:34.380
Hmph, we found it first!

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:35.920
Huh? The man from before...

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:37.750
Ah! Malon!

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:41.000
Wrong... That's not Malon.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.710
What did you say?!

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.130
This isn't the one in the photo.

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:47.750
Then this...!

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:49.540
You're right!

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:51.000
So, then that's...?

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:55.960
Uh... This here is not Malon. This is Matsutaro.

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:58.460
Hey! Don't go leaving me behi-

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:00.460
Oh, it's you...

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:01.630
You know him?

00:16:01.630 --> 00:16:04.670
Yes, he's the client in our current case.

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:05.380
Eh?!

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:07.210
It was a miss.

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:13.420
My late wife and I bought Malon together.

00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:15.130
With your wife...

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:23.920
Systems with a pair of robots that call out and
respond to each other were popular with young lovers.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:28.790
I looked after Matsutaro here, and Malon was my wife's.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:33.290
Thanks to them, my wife and I
came together and made a home.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:38.750
The two of us often took them out for walks
at this very university...

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:40.790
But one day, Malon...

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:42.960
...just disappeared, right?

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:44.460
Yes.

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:51.880
Not long after, my wife passed away,
and then all I was left with was Matsutaro here.

00:16:53.830 --> 00:17:00.920
At that moment, I wanted so badly to get Malon back,
and I desperately searched for the same model, but...

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:07.630
In the end, I never could find one.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:11.080
But just the other day, Matsutaro...

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:14.040
...picked up a response, right? From Malon, I mean.

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:16.170
Exactly.

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:21.830
Surely, Malon is here somewhere
on this university's campus.

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:25.040
Even now she's waiting for us to come.

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:28.580
Please... Please find a way to track her down.

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:32.380
Hmph.

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:35.790
A106, how are you doing narrowing things down?

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:38.380
Thirty-nine hits remaining.

00:17:38.380 --> 00:17:40.170
Alright, off to the next one.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:43.710
Oh, I see, so in the end you're relying on
old-fashioned legwork, huh?!

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:45.000
Shut up!

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:53.670
The protocol that dog robot is using is also being
utilized by mobile devices, so we got over 2,000 hits!

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:56.710
So, we're out here narrowing down that list!

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:02.960
See, I told you! Robots aren't able to do detective work!

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:04.960
This isn't over yet!

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:06.960
Childish...

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:08.000
Look!

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:11.130
We've narrowed it down to 39 hits now!

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:15.960
That's...

00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:17.710
What is it?

00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:18.580
Look!

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:23.790
It largely overlaps with the places
we've already searched, huh?

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:27.920
What? You guys have covered that much ground?

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:30.380
Well, we haven't walked enough to cover 2,000 hits...

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:35.130
These "X" marks are where we searched
and didn't find anything.

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:38.960
In other words, if we cross-reference
my data and this map...

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:42.380
A106!

00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:43.130
Narrow it down!

00:18:43.670 --> 00:18:44.710
Understood.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:48.830
Detected.

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.170
One hit.

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:52.210
Transferring now.

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:54.040
So, where is it?

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:57.040
Huh? Isn't that...?

00:18:57.040 --> 00:18:57.790
What?

00:18:57.790 --> 00:18:59.080
Look, over there.

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:02.880
The spot they've been
doing construction at since last month.

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:07.830
Come to think of it, I believe I saw something on the
bulletin board about underground maintenance work.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:09.670
In that case...

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:11.380
Underground...

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:19.540
Why, of course. We completely overlooked this area.

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:22.330
Whoa, that sure is deep.

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:24.040
It's so dark I can't see anything down there.

00:19:24.210 --> 00:19:26.790
Fifty-two meters to the bottom.

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:28.290
That deep?!

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:31.040
Picking up a response from below.

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:34.040
Alright! I'll head down there
and bring her back up myself!

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:37.290
O-oh! Wh-what now?!

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:39.580
Oxygen concentration: abnormal.

00:19:39.580 --> 00:19:40.880
Say what?!

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:43.540
It's dangerous to head underground
unprepared, you know!

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:45.830
There could also be gas trapped down there!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.460
Well, then what's the plan?!

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:21.460
Target located.

00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:22.960
He did it!

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:25.500
Well done!

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:27.630
What's that...?

00:20:27.630 --> 00:20:29.540
Shock waves from his landing?!

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:30.500
Eh?!

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:33.630
Let's get away from here. It might collapse!

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:40.460
Ran, quickly now!

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:42.460
Six...

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:53.960
Six!

00:21:06.130 --> 00:21:07.130
She moved!

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:14.040
I wonder how Malon was able to
transmit a signal from underground.

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:18.830
Sunlight must have filtered down into the hole.

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:21.250
Then she restarted.

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:24.040
Then the other one must have
received her startup transmission.

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:26.080
But, why was she in that hole in the first place?

00:21:26.210 --> 00:21:27.500
Who knows?

00:21:27.630 --> 00:21:30.710
Nevertheless, because
she arrived here at this university...

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:32.290
...we were able to...

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:33.960
Hey now, you guys!

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:36.830
What? If you're talking about the contest,
I'd say it's a draw.

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:39.420
I sure as heck won't be working for free, anyway!

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:42.290
Give me a break! I'll pay you - don't worry about that!

00:21:43.210 --> 00:21:47.040
So, next time you're in need of a part-time job,
head over to my place.

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:50.540
I'll at least let you make your case.

00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:51.330
Hmph!

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:52.670
Well that's good news!

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:54.330
Thank you.

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:59.290
Things are just like back then...

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:03.130
Back then...

00:22:13.710 --> 00:22:15.210
That's enough to bring tears to your eyes?

00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:21.080
In the end, they went back to acting
like the pets they were programmed to be.

00:22:24.290 --> 00:22:27.290
I'm so glad that in the end the two of them
were paired up again.

00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:33.170
Are you even listening?! How absurd!
Come on, these are robots we're talking about here!

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:34.330
Be quiet.

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:39.710
Keep it down for their sake.

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:43.790
Just what are robots really?

00:22:45.580 --> 00:22:49.790
People have continued asking that for many years,
but it is a question with no answer.

00:22:50.380 --> 00:22:53.000
But, there is one thing I can say:

00:22:53.750 --> 00:22:59.540
These robots were absolutely irreplaceable
in the eyes of that man.

00:23:03.250 --> 00:23:08.580
In a small room in the middle of the debris

00:23:09.290 --> 00:23:14.920
Our thoughts illuminate the whole world

00:23:15.130 --> 00:23:19.960
Possibilities that go on infinitely

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:29.750
Ah, the incipient light is starting to move

00:23:32.750 --> 00:23:38.420
The early afternoon that brought a big dream

00:23:38.420 --> 00:23:45.920
I could see hope in the sky that I looked up into

00:23:46.670 --> 00:23:49.540
Always, always

00:23:50.040 --> 00:23:52.710
It is good to be frantic

00:23:52.710 --> 00:23:58.500
Stand shoulder-to-shoulder with me and let's head toward tomorrow

00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:01.540
Anything, anything

00:24:01.830 --> 00:24:04.670
We should be able to do it

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:13.960
The future we will create however we please

00:24:31.580 --> 00:24:32.580
Of course!

00:24:32.580 --> 00:24:33.830
What are you talking about all of a sudden?

00:24:33.830 --> 00:24:38.000
At the Nerima University Campus Festival,
we at Lab 7 will compete by selling udon noodles!

00:24:38.210 --> 00:24:40.380
And we will call it "Robot Udon!"

00:24:40.380 --> 00:24:43.130
You're not actually thinking of having Six
serve up the udon, are you?

00:24:43.130 --> 00:24:45.960
It's Robot Udon precisely because it'll be
made by a robot. Who else is gonna make it?!

00:24:45.960 --> 00:24:48.380
We're gonna rake in the dough and
score some research funds!

00:24:48.380 --> 00:24:50.130
Next time on ATOM THE BEGINNING:

00:24:50.130 --> 00:24:51.790
"Welcome to Nerima U Festival"!

00:24:51.790 --> 00:24:54.460
A106, make that udon!
